 "notes": {
  "method": "Muristan block (Greek Orthodox market, 1900s): 2 storeys of honey-cream ashlar, ground-floor round-arched shopfronts with fanlights and teal/green steel doors or grey roll-downs, upper floor of round-arched windows and small balconies with black railings (notes 1.6, 1.7, 2.6; F01 from the Redeemer tower shows the blocks and their long red-tile hipped roofs). The face seen straight behind the fountain in D07/D08 is edge 0 (south) plus edge 3 (SW), Review R5.",
  "measured": "D07/D08: ground floor ~5 m (café shopfronts under blue (2016) / maroon (2022) awnings), upper floor with round-arched windows and a balcony with stone posts and black railings across the south face, eaves ~9.5-10 m above the square (people 1.7 m, doors 2.6 m), then the red-tile hip. Height 9.0 above the building ground (its highest corner, -14.58): ~10 m on the south face (ground -15.6).",
  "roof": "Real roof: red-tile hipped (F01, F03, D07, D08). Left flat here: build_city's hip roof uses the oriented bounding box and would overhang this footprint by metres (profile request). 'domes': 1 where set only keeps the vernacular lime-dome field (5-8 domes) off a roof that is really tiled."
 },
